# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment files — never commit.
#
# F-001 (Critical): the production .env was committed in d607028 and pushed to
# GitHub, exposing the database password, mail credentials, Pusher/Reverb keys,
# the reCAPTCHA secret, the HR admin login, API_PROTECT_KEY and APP_KEY.
#
# A tracked .env is also a working hazard: on 2026-09-25 a routine branch
# operation silently replaced a developer's local .env with the committed
# production one, pointing a local `artisan migrate` at production credentials.
# It failed only because that host is unreachable from the dev machine.
#
# Untracking here does NOT rotate the leaked secrets and does NOT remove them
# from history. Both remain open: Q-001 (rotation) and Q-002 (history purge).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database dumps — never commit.
#
# F-002 (Critical): live.sql is a 9.6 MB production dump.
# F-003 (Critical): database/seeders/data/users.sql holds ~1,056 real employee
# records — names, corporate emails, mobile numbers, departments and password
# hashes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/live.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump

